:If it is going to be "us versus them" I guarantee the hackers are going
:to win over the sysadmins. The hackers have the cunning and the initiative.

Don't people get tired of the "poor helpless sysadmin" vs. "evil
genius cracker" schtick?  The one thing that system abusers have over
system administrators is time -- the sysadmin can't afford to focus on
"protect the system" as a goal, because of other imperatives in
his/her job and life, like "make systems usable for people", "have a
life apart from the computer", "appease the boss", etc.  There are
lots of clever sysadmins and stupid systems abusers out there.  The
best sysadmins combine just that magic combination of technical,
clerical, and social bent which could make them quite effective as
systems abusers, if they were to choose that path.

