In fact, I'm posting to this newsgroup from a university in the US, and
I haven't used telnet to any remote site!  My university's News server
doesn't even carry the CAN.XXX or ONT.XXX groups.  

So how am I doing it?  If you are on a Unix workstation, just set your
NNTPSERVER environment variable to some other News server.  Then,
run your News reading software, TIN, TRN, XRN, XVNEWS, RN, NN etc..

The trick is to find News servers that allow remote access via your
News reading software.  Just pay attention to the headers in poster's
messages on the Net.  And give them a try.  Most will refuse access.
But, some will let you in.

