the ones that stick in their minds.

Dean Gopnik said that one of the reasons for trying to get a good
computing policy in place was a particular student disciplinary case
involving computers.  He said, the University had "made a real mess of it."

Jill Presser stated that the current Student Code (Green book)
had a clause giving students all the rights granted by the Canadian
and Quebec charters.  Dean Gopnik, apparently one of the crafters of the
current code, went further to state that the clear intention
of this clause was that the University was choosing
to impose upon itself the same restrictions that apply to the
Government when considering how these rights may be infringed.

